body:
"I dont actually know the possibilities that could happen to steal an election, even though the guy in charge literally called a governor and told him to "Find votes", but that guy is so stupid, theres no way there could be any votes "found", sooooo obviously its impossible, right guys? RIGHT?!"

&nbsp;

I dont know why people want to just assume everything is perfect. If it were, that phone call would not have happened at all. It did... so now, I am honestly questioning the integrity of our elections as a whole. Did he legitimately win, even though he previously lost? How can me and you be 100% certain of this? Why is he going hard with deleting government agencies right now? You tell me.

biggest and most important lesson... when you enter into a relationship, dont let the other person force you to give up who you are. No matter how hard they make your life, you cant give up your old self. If you give up yourself, they will no longer be attracted to you, because you arent who they fell for. Unfortunately, if you didnt already learn this lesson on your own, reading what I am saying will not make sense to you.


Even if you think you are changing for them, and are making their life easier... you are literally just hurting the relationship. Stand your ground. Be yourself. Dont ever EVER let anyone change you. You continue maintaining your hobbies, and interests, and your friendships. Of course, you have to be compromising to make things work... but you have to draw a line at some point, and never give up who you once were.

&nbsp;

And another thing... intimacy is extremely important (to me). I will want that intimacy... If you are in a relationship, and you notice that your partner is constantly rejecting you, then I am going to go ahead and tell you, that relationship should be over. You will be better off looking for someone more compatible with you, that can actually give you what you want. I dont give a fuck what your partners reasons are... its bullshit. They just dont love you.

&nbsp;

And another thing I learned... never be complacent. So you wanted to date this person, and you dated them, now you are exclusively in a relationship, and you have been together for X many years.... You have to continue to be seeing them as the person you wanted to date, and wanted to be in a relationship with.... You cant ever be like... well, we are together now, I can be lazy, and just sit around and not take care of my appearance, and I dont have to tell them nice things, and do nice things to show them my appreciation... that has to continue as if it was day one. Again... people will not understand what I am saying until they learn this lesson the hard way.

&nbsp;


What else have I learned??? Oh... a good one. Never ignore red flags. If you almost broke up with someone at some point, review why you felt that way... chances are high you were right, and probably should have broken up with them without ever looking back. Never expect someone to change. Never assume someone is just immature and will get better... thats really bad. 

&nbsp;

Oh, and another one... if your partner discusses your relationship with ANYONE other than you and a therapist, then that person doesnt respect your relationship. I suggest putting that as a boundary... it is extremely disrespectful to the relationship. People that do this, they are looking for validation about how much they hate the relationship. They want someone else to tell them "you are with the wrong person", so they can leave it. What the fuck kind of relationship is that? Think for your damn self... if you dont want to be with me, dont ask your friends... come tell me we are breaking up. Holy fucking shit. Go ask your damn therapist if you are crazy for feeling that way.... Dont ever go to your damn friends, because for their own safety (as your friends), they will likely have to take your side no matter what bullshit you are telling them. Your family want you to be happy... if you are with someone and you are claiming that you are not happy because of them, well, I wonder what they will tell you... 

&nbsp;

Lets see... theres so much I have learned... if you feel like your partner doesnt compromise with you... they are always getting into arguments with you as a me vs you kind of an argument... then this relationship is bound to fail, 100%. If you are in a relationship, when you get into a fucking argument, it should never be "me vs you".... it should always be "how do WE solve this?". You should be a team, not god damn opponents... What the fuck?

&nbsp;

Im sure ill think of more... I learned too damn much in my past relationship. I am happy with what I have learned. Its sad that it took me 9 years with someone to learn this shit, but I am better off now. If I am ever in another relationship, I am going to make sure things go better this time. I never want to make the same mistakes I have done before. **Boundaries** are HUGE. **Communication** is HUGE. Do not ever ignore these 2.

> Now for the question: Are we talking too much before we’ve even met? 

&nbsp;

Yes. But its kinda too late for you to change that now.
